<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-6835] ODBC driver should handle ungraceful tcp disconnects</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6835</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;It is found that ungraceful TCP disconnect makes ODBC driver stuck at socket recv().&lt;br/&gt;
Ungraceful TCP disconnect could be caused:&lt;br/&gt;
1. Network failure (or new firewall rules)&lt;br/&gt;
2. Remote party shutdown (Half Closed Connection)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, the proposal is:&lt;br/&gt;
setup socket  options: &lt;br/&gt;
1) SO_KEEPALIVE enabled&lt;br/&gt;
2) TCP_KEEPIDLE to 60 sec. It is 2 hour by default&lt;br/&gt;
3) TCP_KEEPINTVL to 1 sec. It is 1 sec at Win and 75 sec at Linux by default.&lt;br/&gt;
4) send/receive buffers to some greater value (8k by default)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
